  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING HUMAN TIGER CO-EXISTENCE IN WESTERN TERAI LANDSCAPE IN NEPAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO MAINTAIN HUMAN LARGE CARNIVORE COEXISTENCE IN THE LANDSCAPE WHILE BRINGING MULTIPLE CONSERVATION BENEFITS TO THE LOCAL COMMUNITIES. THE OBJECTIVES ARE AS FOLLOWS: (1) SET UP A WELL-EQUIPPED AND DEDICATED TEAM FOR PROBLEM TIGER MONITORING AND RESCUE OPERATIONS (2) DEVELOP SHOWCASE MODEL FOR THE PROTECTION OF LIVESTOCK FROM TIGER ATTACK (3) ORGANIZE BEHAVIOR CHANGE TIGER CONSERVATION CAMPAIGN (4) RESTORE DEGRADED FOREST PATCHES IN THE BUFFER ZONES AND FOREST CORRIDORS (5) INITIATE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOOD OPTIONS AND (6) STRENGTHEN COOPERATION BETWEEN INDIA AND NEPAL ON TIGER CONSERVATION.</narrative>
  </description>
